// spec: at namespace scope `T name(100, 200)` declares a function (design.md 22), so a value in its parentheses is an error that says how a variable is written (`T name{...}` or `T name = T(...)`), where it said only "expected parameter type"
// error: namespace_object_with_parentheses_is_error.kpp:8: error: expected parameter type: at namespace and class scope `T name(...)` declares a function; write a variable `T name{...}` or `T name = T(...)` (design.md 22)
template<class A, class B> struct Duo
{
  A a;
  B b;
};
constexpr Duo<int, int> t(100, 200);
int main()
{
  return 0;
}
